{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST System Factory.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST System Factory.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender ghost system factory blender ghost system factory","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST System Factory.md","fileName":"Blender GHOST System Factory.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender GHOST System Factory","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender GHOST Windowing]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender GHOST Windowing","Blender GHOST C API","Blender GHOST Handle","Blender GHOST Window Creation","Blender GHOST Platform Class","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST System Factory.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST System Factory.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender ghost system factory blender ghost system factory","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST System Factory.md","fileName":"Blender GHOST System Factory.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender GHOST System Factory","heading":"Blender GHOST System Factory","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The GHOST system factory creates the singleton object that represents the current operating system. A protected interface constructor prevents arbitrary direct instantiation, while `createSystem()` selects a concrete platform implementation and `getSystem()` retrieves the established instance.\n\nThis design concentrates the platform decision in one place. The [[Blender GHOST C API]] returns a [[Blender GHOST Handle]] for the system, after which calls such as [[Blender GHOST Window Creation]] dispatch through the chosen [[Blender GHOST Platform Class]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender GHOST Windowing","Blender